---
description: Project structure & naming conventions.
globs:
  - "src/**/*"
  - "configs/*.yaml"
---

## Purpose
Keep the codebase predictable with clear module layout and consistent naming.

## Applies When
- Files matched by globs above under `src/` and `configs/`.

## Project Structure
- Models: `src/model/v{X}.py` (factory functions per version)
- Training: `src/training/train_v{X}.py` (base trainer class + concrete trainers)
- Evaluation: `src/evaluation/evaluate_v{X}_model.py`
- Utilities: `src/utils.py`
- Configs: `configs/*.yaml`

## Naming
- Modules/files: snake_case; Classes: PascalCase; Functions/vars: snake_case; Constants: UPPER_SNAKE.
- Use `v{X}` consistently across code, configs, and checkpoints.

## Imports
- Use absolute imports from project root; avoid relative dot-chains.
